.TH ZONEOUT 1
.SH NAME
zoneout \- tank shooter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/zoneout
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ZoneOut
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Games/ZoneOut.HC
tank shooter.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
It opens with Terry Davis's own dialog \-
.RB \(lq "I refuse to rip-off the original, so this is intentionally crappy" \(rq
\- which any key dismisses, starting the clock.
Ten enemy tanks wander a plain under a scrolling horizon.
Turn, drive and shoot them all; the elapsed time is scored and the
best kept between runs.
.PP
Tanks and shots are the original's own mesh sprites, drawn through
.IR draw3d (2)
with a depth buffer, and the horizon is its 1280-pixel panorama tiled
three times so it scrolls seamlessly through a full turn.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B "any key"
Dismiss the opening dialog
.TP
.B Left
Turn left
.TP
.B Right
Turn right
.TP
.B Up
Move forward
.TP
.B Down
Move back
.TP
.B space
Fire
.TP
.B Enter
Restart
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /icons/temple/zoneout_1.mesh
Tank, hit tank and shot meshes
.RB ( zoneout_1 ,
.BR zoneout_2 ,
.BR zoneout_3 ).
.TP
.B /icons/temple/zoneout_4.bit
The horizon panorama, with its
.B .mask
alongside.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/zoneout.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original's File and Play pulldown menus are not drawn; every entry
is on a key.
It has no
.B wasd
alternatives to the arrow keys, and this port no longer offers them
either.
.PP
A shot leaves the gun at
.BR TANK_HEIGHT ,
which in the original's screen-down coordinates puts it below the
enemy tanks' origins rather than level with their guns, and a tank
within range of a shot is lifted by the distance to it, so it springs
up and settles as the shot arrives.
Both are reproduced as written.
.PP
The original's transform clamps depth to 1 instead of clipping, so
geometry behind the eye is smeared to enormous coordinates;
.IR draw3d (2)
rejects a triangle with a vertex behind the eye instead.
Both put it off the screen.
